# Repository memory (RavByte AMS)

**Do not cold-search the codebase** for features already mapped in `memory/`.

## Every task (before editing)

1. Read `memory/context-index.json` — pick the topic file for your task.
2. Read **`memory/11-shawq-domain-map.md`** for tab wiring, date scopes, data paths, and past mistakes.
3. Read `memory/agent-handoff.md` if resuming work.
4. For shared types/APIs, check `memory/repository-graph.json` or run `agent-memory graph query --file <path>`.

## After structural changes

```bash
npm run memory:maintain
npm run memory:graph   # if imports/routes changed
```

Commit updated `memory/` files in the same PR.

## After completing non-trivial work

```bash
npm run memory:worklog -- --agent cursor --message "<what changed and why>" --files "<comma-separated paths>"
```

Before stopping mid-task, update `memory/agent-handoff.md` or run `worklog handoff`.

## Session memory (agentmemory on Railway)

If `AGENTMEMORY_URL` is set (not localhost), use MCP `memory_smart_search` / `recall` for cross-session facts. If unreachable, rely on `memory/` + `AGENT.md` incidents only.
